.TH KEGG 1 2000-1月 "kegg_category_annotation" "kegg_category_annotation"
.SH NAME
kegg_category_annotation \- Append the KEGG BRITE category annotation to a given dataframe by the KEGG id column.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIkegg_category_annotation(\fBkegg\fR as <generic> Background, 
\fBanno\fR as <generic> dataframe, 
\fBkegg_id\fR as string = "kegg_id", 
\fBclass_field\fR as string = "kegg_class", 
\fBcategory_field\fR as string = "kegg_category", 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Append the KEGG BRITE category annotation to a given dataframe by the KEGG id column.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBkegg\fB \fR\- 
 the KEGG BRITE background model that is used for query the category information of
 the KEGG id, for example the model that is created by \fBKO.background\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBanno\fB \fR\- 
 the target dataframe that contains the KEGG id column, the annotation columns will be
 appended to this dataframe directly.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBkegg_id\fB \fR\- the column name of the KEGG id in the **anno** dataframe. Default \fBkegg_id\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBclass_field\fB \fR\- the column name of the output KEGG class information. Default \fBkegg_class\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcategory_field\fB \fR\- the column name of the output KEGG category information. Default \fBkegg_category\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the given dataframe with two new columns (\fBkegg_class\fR and \fBkegg_category\fR) appended,
 or an error message when the required KEGG id column is missing.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Only the first KEGG id will be used when the value of the \fBkegg_id\fR column contains
 multiple ids that are separated by \fB;\fR, \fB/\fR or other blank characters.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
kegg
.SH FILES
.PP
gseakit.dll
.PP
